# (HELMS forge-fix i2) begin (forge fix 2, the owner: "snout helms look alike at 1x; make the variants bolder"): `when
# helmfam-snout,<mass>` replace views, one bold outline per body-mass class (the first replacing view that holds wins).
# the hounskull: a pointed skull, the visor a plate narrowing to the chin, eye slits split by its ridge, on a dark mail
# bell that flares past the jaw; the tall hounskull: a bascinet stretched up into a point leaning back, a long snout;
# the rondel bascinet: a round skull, a short blunt snout with one slit band, a riveted disc at each ear.
# Written by the HELMS area tools/d2.py (D R drawn; U is D with the face details dropped; L is R mirrored and re-lit).
